    "authorAssociation": "NONE",
    "body": "Been using and loving the various mini modules for some time. Recently rewrote my Lazy config to be more consistent and readable. You can see my 'mini' section beginning on line [83](https://github.com/hunleyd/neovim/blob/main/lua/hunleyd/lazy.lua#L83). It works well. However, I cannot get mini.icons to work unless I add it separately (line [217](https://github.com/hunleyd/neovim/blob/main/lua/hunleyd/lazy.lua#L217)). I'm fairly certain I'm just being dumb and the config can be reworked to match the rest of my 'mini' section, but I'm at a loss. Anyone care to help a brother out?",
    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Been using and loving the various mini modules for some time. Recently rewrote my Lazy config to be more consistent and readable. You can see my 'mini' section beginning on line <a href=\"https://github.com/hunleyd/neovim/blob/main/lua/hunleyd/lazy.lua#L83\">83</a>. It works well. However, I cannot get mini.icons to work unless I add it separately (line <a href=\"https://github.com/hunleyd/neovim/blob/main/lua/hunleyd/lazy.lua#L217\">217</a>). I'm fairly certain I'm just being dumb and the config can be reworked to match the rest of my 'mini' section, but I'm at a loss. Anyone care to help a brother out?</p>",
    "bodyText": "Been using and loving the various mini modules for some time. Recently rewrote my Lazy config to be more consistent and readable. You can see my 'mini' section beginning on line 83. It works well. However, I cannot get mini.icons to work unless I add it separately (line 217). I'm fairly certain I'm just being dumb and the config can be reworked to match the rest of my 'mini' section, but I'm at a loss. Anyone care to help a brother out?",
